3. 養聲

廣東話：歌手開演唱會之前，一定要好好養聲，唔好亂叫亂喊。
English: Singers must take good care of their voices before a concert and avoid shouting or screaming.

4. 票尾

廣東話：你睇下張戲飛嘅票尾仲有冇，唔好弄丟咗，因為嗰度有座位號。
English: Check if the ticket stub is still there; don't lose it because the seat number is on it.

5. hacker

廣東話：最近好多公司都擔心俾 hacker 入侵，所以加強咗網絡保安。
English: Recently, many companies are worried about being hacked, so they have strengthened their network security.

6. 石斛蘭

廣東話：呢盆石斛蘭開花咗，佢依附喺樹皮上面生長，真係好靚。
English: This Dendrobium orchid has bloomed; it grows attached to the tree bark and looks really beautiful.

7. 吊詭 (矛盾、悖論)

廣東話：佢話自己最鍾意安靜，但係又成日去最嘈嘅夜店，真係好吊詭。
English: He says he loves silence the most, but he always goes to the noisiest nightclubs; it's really paradoxical.

8. 吊詭 (似非而是、荒謬)

廣東話：呢個社會有好多吊詭嘅現象，例如越係講求誠信，越多人講大話。
English: There are many absurd phenomena in this society, for example, the more people talk about integrity, the more people lie.

9. 各為其主

廣東話：雖然佢哋兩個喺球場上鬥得好兇，但其實佢哋都係各為其主，盡力為球隊爭勝。
English: Although they fought fiercely on the court, they were actually each serving their own master, doing their best to win for their teams.

10. 軨蓋

廣東話：部車撞親牆角，搞到個軨蓋都爆開咗，要即刻去車房執返。
English: The car hit the corner of the wall, causing the wheel cover to pop off; we need to go to the garage to fix it immediately.

11. 打哥夫

廣東話：阿爸成日話要去打哥夫，其實佢只係鍾意同啲朋友喺草地傾偈。
English: Dad always says he's going to play golf, but actually, he just likes chatting with his friends on the grass.

12. 免揀

廣東話：呢間舖頭賣嘅水果全部係免揀，買幾多就幾多，唔可以挑挑揀揀。
English: All the fruits sold in this shop are "no selection allowed"; you buy what you get and can't pick and choose.

13. 擺闊佬

廣東話：佢明明冇幾多錢，仲要擺闊佬請客食飯，結果搞到要借錢還卡數。
English: He clearly doesn't have much money, but he still puts on airs and treats everyone to dinner, ending up having to borrow money to pay off his credit card.

14. 廣播劇

廣東話：阿嫲以前最鍾意聽廣播劇，每晚八點鐘都會準時坐喺收音機前面。
English: Grandma used to love listening to radio dramas; she would sit in front of the radio at 8 PM sharp every night.

15. 錄影機

廣東話：細個嗰陣，我哋用部錄影機錄低咗好多卡通片嚟睇。
English: When I was little, we used a video recorder to record a lot of cartoons to watch.

16. 吟詩吟唔甩

廣東話：佢偷嘢俾人捉住，仲想狡辯，但係監控錄像拍得清清楚楚，真係吟詩吟唔甩。
English: He was caught stealing and tried to make excuses, but the surveillance footage was crystal clear; he really couldn't deny it.

17. 佈道大會

廣東話：上個週末，教會舉行咗一個大型嘅佈道大會，嚟咗好多信徒。
English: Last weekend, the church held a large evangelistic rally, and many believers came.

18. 寫手 (寫作的人)

廣東話：佢係一個自由寫手，靠寫專欄同小說過活。
English: He is a freelance writer, making a living by writing columns and novels.

19. 寫手 (代筆)

廣東話：嗰個名人嘅自傳其實唔係佢自己寫，係請咗個寫手代筆。
English: That celebrity's autobiography wasn't actually written by him; he hired a ghostwriter to write it.

20. 代打

廣東話：我唔想打呢個副本，太難打，不如搵個高手幫我代打啦。
English: I don't want to do this dungeon; it's too hard. Maybe I should find an expert to carry me through it.

21. 茶碗

廣東話：呢個茶碗係日本買返嚟嘅，手感好重，飲茶嗰陣特別有感覺。
English: This tea bowl was bought from Japan; it feels heavy in the hand and gives a special feeling when drinking tea.

22. 茶隔

廣東話：沖普洱嗰陣記得用茶隔，唔好俾啲碎茶葉入咗杯度。
English: Remember to use a tea strainer when brewing Pu'er tea; don't let the broken tea leaves get into the cup.

23. 只許州官放火，不准百姓點燈

廣東話：老細自己遲到就話有事，我哋遲一分鐘就扣糧，真係只許州官放火，不准百姓點燈。
English: The boss is late and says he has a reason, but if we are one minute late, our pay gets docked; it's really "do as I say, not as I do" (double standards).

24. 獨唱

廣東話：今次表演佢唔係合唱，而係一個人獨唱，壓力好大。
English: In this performance, he isn't singing in a chorus but singing solo, which puts a lot of pressure on him.

25. 快人快事

廣東話：佢係個快人快事嘅人，講完就即刻去做，唔會拖泥帶水。
English: He is a straightforward and decisive person; once he says something, he does it immediately without dragging his feet.

26. 四腳獸

廣東話：嗰間公廁成日俾人話係「四腳獸」出沒嘅地方，好多人都不敢入去。
English: That public restroom is often rumored to be a place where "four-legged beasts" (couples having sex) hang out, so many people are afraid to go in.

27. 無米粥

廣東話：而家只係初步傾吓合作意向，仲係煲緊無米粥，未確定具體條款。
English: Right now, we are just discussing preliminary cooperation intentions; it's still just "cooking porridge without rice" (a tentative plan), and specific terms haven't been finalized.

28. 義會

廣東話：阿婆以前靠參加義會嚟周轉資金，邊個急用錢就標會，大家互相幫助。
English: Grandma used to rely on participating in rotating savings associations to manage cash flow; whoever needed money urgently would bid for the pot, and everyone helped each other.

29. 榜文

廣東話：古時候官府會將通緝犯嘅資料寫喺榜文上面，貼喺城門口。
English: In ancient times, the government would write the details of wanted criminals on proclamations and post them at the city gates.

30. MK名

廣東話：佢個網名叫做「堅系°唯愛°小龍」，真係好典型嘅 MK名。
English: His online name is "Jian Shi ° Wei Ai ° Xiao Long" (Definitely ° Only Love ° Little Dragon), which is a very typical MK name. [end of text]


